<p>President Trump&#x27;s envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner are traveling to Islamabad for a new push to revive diplomacy over the nearly eight-week Iran war, with Iran&#x27;s Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi already in Pakistan on a regional tour. The White House said the US team wants to keep moving toward a deal, and several reports said Vice President JD Vance is not traveling for now but remains on standby if negotiations advance. One encouraging sign is that diplomatic channels are still open, even though the format remains disputed. Washington has described the Islamabad effort as an in-person conversation with Iranian representatives, but Tehran has publicly ruled out direct talks during this visit and said Pakistan may instead pass messages between the sides. The talks matter far beyond the meeting room because a fragile ceasefire is still holding while core disputes over the Strait of Hormuz, nuclear restrictions and the sequencing of concessions remain unresolved, with wider implications for regional stability and global energy flows.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/bL9brY_RGIlbH8wXIb92GRf9Xjrsdh4xqLdXh2YEWYikuTqORUAVero1SXHg_ZCd3009ctkokjUPuaNR7LDz8e3AZTpxHrnMy4gIdIYBzenZbQsUraBwLHz60dzZvi96xpgYsKxUPm--z9nupu-GVhjBFybT54m41w53Cyjh5jIXiIhNcCrPj54Egah7UGPqUz7tP5R5GDR85GMnevUpuQ' alt='Tehran on Thursday. Iran’s foreign minister was expected to meet with Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner in Pakistan this weekend.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Pakistan mediation: Pakistani officials were set to host and facilitate contacts, and Deputy Prime Minister Ishaq Dar said he hoped for &quot;meaningful engagements&quot; to support regional peace and stability.</li><li>Iranian message: Several reports said Araghchi was carrying or conveying Tehran&#x27;s formal response to US proposals that Pakistan had previously helped relay, suggesting negotiations have continued through back channels even while direct meetings remain uncertain.</li><li>Regional itinerary: Araghchi described his trip to Islamabad, Muscat and Moscow as a tour to coordinate with partners on bilateral matters and regional developments, showing that Iran is pairing any Pakistan diplomacy with consultations in Oman and Russia.</li><li>Security backdrop: Islamabad was under lockdown as delegations arrived, underscoring how sensitive the talks are and how high the political stakes remain around any renewed US-Iran engagement.</li><li>EU concern: EU foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas warned that any agreement focused only on politics without nuclear experts could end up weaker than the original JCPOA and leave &quot;a more dangerous Iran&quot;.</li></ul><blockquote>We’ve certainly seen some progress from the Iranian side in the last couple of days - Karoline Leavitt</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House: Karoline Leavitt said Witkoff and Kushner would go to Pakistan to &quot;hear the Iranians out,&quot; while President Trump, the vice president and the secretary of state would stay in the US for updates. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/24/kushner-witkoff-iran-pakistan-00890912'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Iranian Foreign Ministry: Spokesman Esmaeil Baqaei said no meeting with the United States was planned during Araghchi&#x27;s Pakistan visit and that Tehran would instead convey its views to Pakistan. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639043-iran-pakistan-us-talks/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: Pakistani officials cast Araghchi&#x27;s visit as part of a push for regional peace and stability and received him with senior civilian and military leaders, signaling Islamabad&#x27;s intent to play an active intermediary role. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1994917/araghchis-islamabad-visit-bodes-well-for-us-dialogue'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>European Union: Kaja Kallas argued that any renewed Iran agreement should include nuclear experts, warning that a narrower process could produce a weaker deal than the JCPOA. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/24/iran-war-live-updates-trump-hormuz-strait-israel-lebanon-truce'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/24/iran-war-live-updates-trump-hormuz-strait-israel-lebanon-truce'>US envoy and Trump’s son-in-law to travel to Pakistan amid hopes for renewed Iran peace talks – as it happened</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/us-iran-war-trump-strait-of-hormuz-hezbollah-lebanon-israel-ceasefire/'>Witkoff, Kushner to take part in second round of Iran peace talks in Pakistan</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-israel-war-usa-west-asia-conflict-peace-talks-in-pakistan-live-updates-april-25-2026/article70904298.ece'>Israel-Iran war LIVE: Egyptian and Pakistani officials discuss Iran war</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639043-iran-pakistan-us-talks/'>Tehran denies new talks with Trump’s envoys</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1994917/araghchis-islamabad-visit-bodes-well-for-us-dialogue'>Araghchi’s Islamabad visit ‘bodes well’ for US dialogue</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/middle-east-crisis/article/2026/04/24/iran-s-top-diplomat-travels-to-pakistan-as-ceasefire-talks-with-washington-remain-stalled_6752796_368.html'>US hopes for progress, but Iran says no direct talks</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/25/whats-at-stake-for-iran-and-the-us-in-islamabad'>What’s at stake for Iran and the US in Islamabad?</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/25/nx-s1-5799372/iran-middle-east-updates'>Iran&#x27;s foreign minister awaits U.S. delegation to Pakistan for peace talks</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/a0b83a1d-78d3-4097-a5a7-fbc11b250f5e'>Witkoff and Kushner to travel to Islamabad as hopes rise for Iran peace talks</a> - ft.com</